use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Announcement import Announcement
from ../../../behaviors/Dragging import Dragging

export ui-component ImageCropper:
    description:
        An image cropper lets the user choose which part of an image to keep,
        such as when setting a profile photo. The user moves and resizes a
        crop area over the image, and can zoom, rotate, and flip the image
        underneath it.

    behaviors:
        - @{Dragging}
        - @{Announcement}

    cropArea:
        The crop area is a rectangle or a circle, with the part of the image
        outside it dimmed. The user drags the area to move it, and drags its
        edges or corners to resize it. It always stays within the image, and
        between the smallest and largest size the component allows.

    shape:
        The component can fix the crop area's proportions, such as square or
        16 by 9, and resizing keeps them. Whether the user can hold a key to
        keep the current proportions while resizing is up to the chosen
        library.

    fixedArea:
        Instead, the component can fix the crop area in place, so the user
        moves and zooms the image underneath it, as many profile photo
        croppers do.

    image:
        The user can drag the image to move it, and zoom with the scroll wheel
        or by pinching, towards wherever the pointer or fingers are. The
        component can offer controls to rotate and flip it. Zoom and rotation
        stay within limits the component sets.

    keyboard:
        The crop area can be focused. The arrow keys move it by a small step,
        and by a bigger step with a modifier held. Other keys resize it and
        zoom the image in and out. Which keys, and the size of each step, is
        up to the chosen library.

    announcing:
        Assistive tools are told the crop area's position and size, and the
        image's zoom and rotation, as they change.

    starting:
        The component can set where the crop area starts, and the starting
        zoom, rotation, and flip. It can also set any of them later.

    result:
        The component is told the crop as it changes. The crop can be given in
        the original image's own pixels, with zoom, rotation, and flip taken
        into account, so the same crop can be applied to the full-size image
        elsewhere, such as on a server. The cropper can also produce the
        cropped image itself, which is never enlarged beyond the original's
        resolution.

    nonGoals:
        - No other editing, such as filters, brightness, or drawing
        - It doesn't choose or upload the image. A FilePicker or DropZone can
            supply it, and the app uploads the result
